# Build and disposable runtime artifacts
build/
scratch/
.venv/

# INPUTS come from YOUR OWN disc and are never committed: the disc image and anything extracted from
# it are Activision's/Traveller's Tales', not this repo's.
#
# Kept NARROW on purpose. Everything extracted lands under scratch/ (already ignored above); the
# patterns here are the belt to that braces, for a file dropped in the repo root. Broad patterns
# (*.bin, *.raw, *.all, *.dat) would be actively wrong here — this game's entire asset set uses those
# extensions, so they would also match ordinary PROSE naming those files in docs, which floods
# tools/go_public.py's "docs referencing gitignored items" check with false positives, and a gate that
# cries wolf is one people stop reading. `SLUS_008.93` is deliberately NOT listed for the same reason:
# every doc in this repo names it in prose. go_public.py's CONFIG lists it as a copyright PATH pattern
# instead, where it matches paths and not prose.
*.chd
.env

# The framework. Not tracked: either a symlink to the workspace shared clone (local) or a
# private clone at psxport.pin (fresh machine). Managed by tools/psxport_sync.py.
/external/psxport
*.log

# Python bytecode — never committed. Compiled .pyc embed ABSOLUTE SOURCE PATHS, i.e. a machine-path
# leak that a TEXT-only audit cannot see, because they are binary.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor / OS noise
compile_commands.json
.DS_Store
